      "content": "untanned skins of squirrels | the fur of one or other of various species of slender, graceful, agile rodents (characterized by a long bushy tail, furry coat, and bright eyes), belonging to the genus Sciurus, or to the widely-distributed sub-family Sciurina including this; especially the common species Sciurus vulgaris, native to Britain, Europe, and parts of Asia. (OED s.v. squirrel n.) | one or other of various species of slender, graceful, agile rodents (characterized by a long bushy tail, furry coat, and bright eyes), belonging to the genus Sciurus, or to the widely-distributed sub-family Sciurina including this; especially the common species Sciurus vulgaris, native to Britain, Europe, and parts of Asia. (OED s.v. squirrel n.)"
    }
